At some point, Acidheart was used by [[Klaus]] against [[Dante Vale]] so that Klaus could return to his experiments for [[the Organization]]. {{source|SAS-127}}

Acidheart was used by [[Rassimov]] to attack [[Lok Lambert]] during the [[Huntik Foundation]]'s assault on [[the Professor's castle]], effectively cutting Rassimov's opposition down to just [[Dante Vale]]. {{source|The Divine Comedy}}

In the hunt for the [[Willblade]] in [[Avalon]], [[Wilder]] targeted Lok with Acidheart, but the spell was reflected with [[Armorbrand]]. After Lok acquired the Willblade, Wilder again tried to hit Lok with Acidheart, but the spell was negated by the Willblade. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}

Acidheart was used point-blank by [[Tantras]] when he deduced that [[Zhalia Moon]] was a spy. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}

During the assault on the [[Fortress of Iron Will]], a [[Casterwill Hunter]] used the spell on [[LeBlanche]], injuring him. Later, Tantras again used this spell to attack [[Sophie Casterwill]] and to buy time for [[Kiel]]. {{source|The Spiral War}}

* Acidheart debuted in "[[The Divine Comedy]]" with a translucent violet aura and was nearly identical to [[Drybite]]. The coloration of Acidheart was changed for every subsequent appearance.
* In "[[Chasing Void]]", Wilder casting Acidheart in the previous episode re-appears as a flashback, though neither Lok nor [[Cherit]] witnessed it.

